 price the policy rate at 4.50% through 2027Q1 and 4.25% by mid-2027. They reach 4.00% by 2027Q4, so the market is pricing about 50bp of cuts. Governor Ashby's base case is a single 25bp cut in 2027. She said markets \"may be getting ahead of themselves.\"\n- **Sensitivity:** The factsheet says VLTX's holdings are long-duration growth names. Each 50bp lower on the policy path has historically added about 1.5 points to the basket's P/E. The basket trades at 19x forward earnings.\n- **If the CMA is right:** Only half the priced easing happens, which is 25bp short of the market. That would take roughly 0.75 points off the multiple, about 4% (19x to about 18.25x). That is a modest risk and it is already partly in the market's expectations.\n- **Earnings:** Consensus expects 2027 EPS growth of 14%, driven by backlog conversion at Voltaris and Tarnwell. Estimates have risen 3% over the past quarter. 14% growth outweighs a roughly 4% multiple compression, so the holdings still show positive net earnings-driven upside. The risk is that the multiple stops expanding, not that it collapses.\n- **Caveats:**\n  - The 1.5-point sensitivity is a historical rule of thumb.\n  - Voltaris (14%) and Tarnwell (11%) are 25% of the fund between them, so any backlog slip would hit earnings hard.\n  - I didn't check the options pricing here. n3 is covering that.","ttft_ms":1972,"type":"result","duration_ms":24691,"uuid":"59bf5b71-76b5-472a-940f-e1729d789f54","ttft_stream_ms":1235,"time_to_request_ms":375,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":27,"system_prompt":8,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":8,"input_attachments":32,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":31,"tool_pool_refresh":14,"init_message":35,"init_frame_send":11,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":11,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":18,"request_announcements":114,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":12,"message_normalization":5,"client_creation":27,"request_build":10},"turn_st